----|\n| G1 [ ] | `merge_sort` | `a = NULL`, `b = NULL`, `size = 0` | child-process status must exactly match C |\n| G2 [ ] | `merge_sort` | `a = NULL`, valid `b`, `size = 1` | child-process status must exactly match C |\n| G3 [ ] | `merge_sort` | valid `a`, `b = NULL`, `size = 1` | child-process status must exactly match C |\n| G4 [ ] | `merge_sort` | `a = NULL`, `b = NULL`, `size = -1` | child-process status must exactly match C |\n| G5 [ ] | `merge_sort` | `a = NULL`, `b = NULL`, `size = INT_MAX` | child-process status must exactly match C |\n\nThere are no public enum parameters and no documented bounded value range, so\nout-of-range enum and one-past-documented-range cases are not applicable.\n# Configuration surface\n\nMechanical source axes:\n\n- Public entry points: `merge_sort` only.\n- Runtime options, modes, flags, formats, element types, and byte-order\n  choices: none.\n- Input shape branch: recursion stops when `hi - lo <= 1`; larger inputs split\n  at `(lo + hi) / 2`, making odd and even counts distinct shapes.\n- Merge branches: take the left item when its `sort_bits` is less than or equal\n  to the right item's value; otherwise take the right item; take the remaining\n  left side after the right side is exhausted.\n- Although the source contains a `texture_id` tie comparison, the preceding\n  `sort_bits <=` branch already returns for equality, so equal `sort_bits`\n  always preserve left-before-right order regardless of `texture_id`.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `merge_sort` | empty input (`size = 0`) | [ ] |\n| 2 | `merge_sort` | singleton input (`size = 1`) | [ ] |\n| 3 | `merge_sort` | two elements with left `sort_bits <=` right | [ ] |\n| 4 | `merge_sort` | two elements with left `sort_bits >` right | [ ] |\n| 5 | `merge_sort` | even count at least four, mixed ordering and merge exhaustion | [ ] |\n| 6 | `merge_sort` |